00:29:40.950 --> 00:29:46.430
Verify there are no gaps because there could be pinholes that you don't see if your welds aren't perfect is you could wait till night

00:29:46.430 --> 00:29:52.999
And then go underneath the car and then shine a light upwards and look for any light leaking through or you could grab a box

00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:57.079
I cut a little hole in it and the box is designed to keep the light out so you can look for those pinholes

00:29:57.300 --> 00:29:59.719
Even during the day so just get a strong LED

00:29:59.790 --> 00:30:03.499
Light and shine it below the metal that you welded and so far so good

00:30:03.500 --> 00:30:05.240
I don't see any light leaking through

00:30:05.240 --> 00:30:10.099
There's no pinholes and then if I bring my light down here at the bottom where that factory hole is don't worry

00:30:10.100 --> 00:30:13.940
We're gonna fill that with a plastic grommet when we're done. But if we bring it back here check that out

00:30:13.940 --> 00:30:17.869
You see those two pin holes right at the bottom right there. That's what you're gonna look for

00:30:17.870 --> 00:30:21.650
That's two small holes that we would have otherwise missed if we didn't use this method

00:30:21.650 --> 00:30:25.849
So we need to make sure we fill those and just to give you an idea of what it looks like in the daylight

00:30:25.850 --> 00:30:32.719
There's the first small hole and then there's the second even smaller hole right there. So it's a good little trick and now it's Fillies

00:30:39.450 --> 00:30:41.070
And

00:30:41.070 --> 00:30:44.719
Finally with those two simple welds we have sealed this completely off

00:30:44.720 --> 00:30:50.990
This is welded in and we are done but not completely done. We're done welding now

00:30:51.090 --> 00:30:55.820
What we need to do is we need to seal this we need to paint it so that we don't get rust

00:30:55.820 --> 00:31:00.229
There's always going to be some moisture and some oxygen in the air that could cause this to rust

00:31:00.380 --> 00:31:03.619
So painting is very important and to prep the surface for paint

00:31:03.620 --> 00:31:07.130
We want to get rid of all that loose surface rust which we did in order to weld

00:31:07.130 --> 00:31:08.030
So we're good with that

00:31:08.030 --> 00:31:10.280
Then you want to grab your 80 grit sandpaper

00:31:10.410 --> 00:31:15.649
And we want to send the metal surface to give the paint something to grab onto 80 grit is pretty aggressive

00:31:15.650 --> 00:31:17.280
So it's gonna leave some deeper scratches

00:31:17.280 --> 00:31:23.930
and that paint is gonna be able to adhere to that very well compared to a smooth surface then vacuum up all the dust from

00:31:23.930 --> 00:31:28.729
sanding and finally clean off the surface with alcohol which is going to remove any oils and

00:31:29.060 --> 00:31:33.979
On the metal so that we have a good clean surface for the paint distictive and look at all that dirt

00:31:33.980 --> 00:31:34.890
we removed and

00:31:34.890 --> 00:31:40.759
Now we are ready to paint but never paint out of your container because if you don't use it all the paint in the container

00:31:40.760 --> 00:31:43.910
Is gonna go bad quicker so pour a little paint into the cup

00:31:43.980 --> 00:31:49.490
Trying not to make a mess and a really cool trick to seal your paint can so it lasts a long time on the shelf

00:31:49.490 --> 00:31:53.150
Grab some plastic wrap and cover the can but leave a little opening

00:31:53.400 --> 00:31:57.830
Then grab one of these compressed air dusters and you want to slowly add air to the can

00:31:57.990 --> 00:32:02.330
The canned air that you're adding is actually r134a a refrigerant

00:32:02.330 --> 00:32:07.999
So it's gonna sink down to the bottom and displace the oxygen since it's heavier oxygen is what makes the paint Harden

00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:13.369
So without the oxygen the paint is gonna be like brand-new the next time you open it now get your paint and spread a thin

00:32:13.370 --> 00:32:17.359
Coat around the entire floorboard making sure to work it into every nook and cranny

00:32:17.360 --> 00:32:23.240
I like to add the paint thick so it covers everything but don't leave it thick make sure you spread it out nice and thin

00:32:23.450 --> 00:32:28.819
All right. So four hours later, we know this is dry because my finger isn't sticking to the paint

00:32:28.820 --> 00:32:34.219
So with the new brush, let's add our second thin coat of paint. And again, make sure this layer is thin

00:32:34.800 --> 00:32:41.300
All right and 24 hours later check this out. Now. It doesn't have to look perfect. But that does look pretty good for something

00:32:41.300 --> 00:32:47.359
That's gonna get covered by carpet the most important thing though is how it functions and this is a special paint

00:32:47.360 --> 00:32:48.500
That's impermeable

00:32:48.500 --> 00:32:53.869
It goes on relatively thick and it creates a barrier between the metal and the air and moisture

00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:58.130
That's gonna prevent rust and it seals in all of our welds as well

00:32:58.130 --> 00:33:02.930
And since we did but welds and not lap welds we don't need to use seam sealer. So this is a job

00:33:02.930 --> 00:33:06.139
Well done, and if you're wondering I sealed under the car as well

00:33:06.140 --> 00:33:08.060
Not only did I paint where we welded

00:33:08.060 --> 00:33:12.019
But I also painted past that that way it seals it off really well

00:33:12.230 --> 00:33:14.840
So our sheet metal is sealed on both sides now

00:33:14.840 --> 00:33:19.789
There's one more thing we need to do and that is install a rubber grommet in the factory hole

00:33:19.790 --> 00:33:24.229
I assumed the previous owner left this undone to let the water drain out, but now we don't need that

00:33:24.230 --> 00:33:27.050
So just push it into place and there you go

00:33:27.050 --> 00:33:32.269
That is how you properly repair a rust hole whether it's in your quarter panel or if it's in your floor

00:33:32.270 --> 00:33:36.349
That is the exact process that you want to follow. I mean check it out

